# Paths of the core, relative to harness/. `./dev sync` copies exactly these (at the chosen revision) into a
# consumer's .harness/. A name ending in / means every tracked file below it. Nothing else under harness/
# is core: a file added there reaches a consumer only once it is listed here.
dev
conf.awk
gate
guard
check-pins
check-dependabot
check-bindings
gh-token.sh
gh-token.md
git-prune-merged.sh
commands
README.md
core.files
bindings/
githooks/
templates/
